<!-- Curriculum sub-strand: Core 1.3, Essential 1.2 -->

<chapter xml:id="ch-compound-proportions-rates-of-work-and-mixtures" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Compound Proportions, Rates of Work and Mixtures</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      In earlier grades you compared quantities using ratios, rates and proportions, for example when sharing profit between partners or working out the cost of several items from the cost of one.
    </p>
    <p>
      In this chapter you will divide quantities into proportional parts and solve problems in which a quantity depends on more than one other quantity. You will work out how long a job takes when people, machines or taps work together at different rates. Finally you will find the quantities, costs and ratios of the ingredients in a mixture.
    </p>
    <p>
      These ideas are used every day in Kenya: planning labour on a building site or a farm, filling and emptying water tanks, and blending tea, animal feed or fertiliser to get the right quality at the right price.
    </p>
  </introduction>

